1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:04,160
Twenty dollar bills beat hundreds here, and your bathroom scale decides it.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,180
So you get one of two piles of free cash.

3
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,960
The first pile is your weight in twenty dollar bills.

4
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:14,240
The second pile is hundred dollar bills, stacked flat, as tall as you.

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:19,180
You said hundreds, right? Tap the heart if you did. No judgment— okay, a little.

6
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,700
Now run it on the average American guy, with CDC numbers.

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:26,940
He weighs one ninety-nine pounds. And every bill weighs about one gram.

8
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:31,300
And he's about sixty-nine inches tall, so that's how high his hundreds stack.

9
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,520
So his weight in twenties is about one point eight million.

10
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:38,320
His height in hundreds is only about one point six million.

11
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,300
Send this to the friend who'd grab hundreds instantly.

12
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:45,000
Wait, why? A pound of twenties is about nine grand.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,260
An inch of hundreds is about twenty-three grand, but you've got way more pounds than inches.

14
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,080
Now here's your cheat code, and it's worth a follow.

15
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:55,620
Take your height in inches, and multiply by two point five six.

16
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:59,720
If you weigh more than that number in pounds, take the twenties.

17
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,280
So what's your bathroom scale saying, twenties or hundreds?
